[00:00.00]Hello everyone, and welcome back to Mr. English Channel. I'm Emily.|大家好，欢迎回到 Mr. English Channel。我是 Emily。
[00:10.26]And I'm Paul. It's great to be here with you all today.|我是 Paul。今天很高兴和大家在一起。
[00:14.08]Yes, it is. Today we have a super interesting topic for our A1 English learners.|是啊。今天我们为 A1 级别的学习者准备了一个非常有意思的话题。
[00:21.02]We're going to talk about something everyone experiences, jobs.|我们要聊一件人人都会经历的事——工作。
[00:25.22]how to describe what you do, your daily work, and even what you hope for in the future.|怎么描述你的工作、你每天做什么，甚至你对未来的期望。
[00:31.84]It's going to be fun.|会很有意思。
[00:33.34]That's right, Emily. Talking about your job is a very common conversation.|没错，Emily。聊工作是极其常见的对话。
[00:38.00]Are you ready to dive into the world of work?|你准备好进入职场世界了吗？
[00:41.10]Absolutely, Emily. Let's get started.|当然，Emily。我们开始吧。
[00:43.86]Okay, so let's imagine someone asks you, what do you do? How do you answer, Paul?|好，想象有人问你「What do you do?」，Paul，你怎么回答？
[00:50.80]Good question, Emily. The easiest way is to say your job title.|好问题，Emily。最简单的方式就是说出你的职位。
[00:55.22]For example, I can say, I'm a teacher. Simple.|比如我可以说「I'm a teacher.」，很简单。
[00:59.48]Yes, that's perfect. Or you can say, I work as a designer. See? Very clear.|对，非常好。或者可以说「I work as a designer.」，看，很清楚。
[01:06.56]So, Paul, what is your job title?|那 Paul，你的职位是什么？
[01:09.26]I'm an English teacher, Emily. I love it. What about you?|我是英语老师，Emily。我很喜欢。你呢？
[01:13.50]I'm a presenter for Mr. English Channel, and I also work as a content creator. It's a fun job.|我是 Mr. English Channel 的主持人，同时也做内容创作。这工作挺有趣。
[01:20.46]That's great. And sometimes people want to know about the company.|很好。有时人们还想知道公司的情况。
[01:25.61]So you can say, I work for a marketing agency.|你可以说「I work for a marketing agency.」
[01:29.20]Or if you work for yourself, you can say, I'm self-employed.|如果是自己干，可以说「I'm self-employed.」
[01:34.06]Exactly. Like me, Paul, sometimes I'm self-employed. It means I am my own boss.|正是。像我，Paul，有时我就是自由职业者，意思是我自己当老板。
[01:41.74]Yes, that's nice. And what about your responsibilities? What do you do every day?|是啊，不错。那你的职责呢？你每天做什么？
[01:47.80]Ah, yes, this is important.|啊对，这很重要。
[01:50.36]You can say, I manage social media.|你可以说「I manage social media.」
[01:53.56]Or, I help customers every day.|或者「I help customers every day.」
[01:56.82]It tells people what your job involves.|这能告诉别人你的工作包含什么。
[01:59.86]Right, so if someone asks me about my responsibilities,|对，所以如果有人问我职责，
[02:03.58]I can say, I prepare lessons and teach English to students.|我可以说「I prepare lessons and teach English to students.」
[02:08.18]That's my main task.|这是我主要的任务。
[02:09.36]Good example.|好例子。
[02:10.74]And we have some useful expressions here.|这里有一些实用表达。
[02:13.78]You can say, I'm responsible for.|你可以说「I'm responsible for...」
[02:16.32]For example, I'm responsible for planning the classes.|比如「I'm responsible for planning the classes.」
[02:20.80]Yes, that's a good one.|对，这个好用。
[02:22.48]Or, my main task is.|或者「My main task is...」
[02:25.18]For me, my main task is to make learning English fun.|对我来说，我的主要任务是让学英语变得有趣。
[02:29.46]Oh, you do a great job at that, Paul.|哦，这点你做得特别好，Paul。
[02:32.90]Thanks, Emily.|谢谢，Emily。
[02:34.38]Another useful phrase is, a typical day at work looks like.|另一个实用说法是「A typical day at work looks like...」
[02:39.52]This helps you describe your daily tasks easily.|这能帮你轻松描述每天的任务。
[02:42.80]Yes, exactly.|对，正是。
[02:43.72]So, if I say, a typical day at work looks like teaching five classes and grading homework, you understand my day.|所以如果我说「A typical day at work looks like teaching five classes and grading homework.」，你就明白我的一天了。
[02:52.98]Perfect!|完美！
[02:53.82]So, remember, you can talk about your job title, the company you work for, and your responsibilities.|记住，你可以聊职位、你所在的公司，以及你的职责。
[03:01.12]Easy peasy.|小菜一碟。
[03:02.16]Okay, Emily, let's move on to the next part.|好，Emily，我们进入下一部分。
[03:05.68]Your daily routine at work.|你在工作中的日常安排。
[03:08.40]People are often curious about what you do from morning to evening.|人们常常好奇你从早到晚都在做什么。
[03:12.98]Yes, it's interesting to know. So first, you can talk about what time you start and finish.|是啊，挺有意思。首先可以聊你几点上班、几点下班。
[03:21.50]For example, I start work at 9 a.m. and finish at 5 p.|比如「I start work at 9 a.m. and finish at 5 p.」
[03:26.55]m.|「m.」（下午五点）
[03:27.24]Simple and clear. What about tasks during the day, like meetings, emails, and other tasks?|简单清楚。那白天的工作呢？比如会议、邮件和其他任务？
[03:34.80]Oh, very important. Many jobs have meetings and emails.|哦，非常重要。很多工作都少不了会议和邮件。
[03:39.63]I can say, every morning I check my emails and attend a short meeting.|我可以说「Every morning I check my emails and attend a short meeting.」
[03:46.34]Yes, that's a classic start to the day for many people.|对，这是很多人一天经典的开始。
[03:50.46]And then you can talk about your main tasks.|然后可以聊你的主要任务。
[03:53.75]Then I work on my main tasks until lunch.|「Then I work on my main tasks until lunch.」
[03:57.52]Exactly. And what about breaks and interactions with colleagues?|正是。那休息和与同事的互动呢？
[04:02.46]Do you have lunch with co-workers? Do you take coffee breaks?|你会和同事一起吃午饭吗？会去喝咖啡休息吗？
[04:07.18]Good point. I can say I usually have lunch with my colleagues at 1 p.m.|说得好。我可以说「I usually have lunch with my colleagues at 1 p.m.」
[04:12.68]or I take a short coffee break in the afternoon.|或者「I take a short coffee break in the afternoon.」
[04:16.64]It adds more detail to your routine.|这样你的日常描述就更细致了。
[04:19.82]It really helps to paint a picture of your day.|确实能帮人「看见」你的一天。
[04:23.24]So a full example could be every morning I check my emails and attend a short meeting.|完整例子可以是：「Every morning I check my emails and attend a short meeting.」
[04:30.80]Then I work on my main tasks until lunch.|「Then I work on my main tasks until lunch.」
[04:34.14]In the afternoon, I have a few more meetings and answer more emails.|「In the afternoon, I have a few more meetings and answer more emails.」
[04:39.32]I usually finish around 5 p.m.|「I usually finish around 5 p.m.」
[04:41.94]That's a great example, Emily.|例子很好，Emily。
[04:43.72]It sounds like a busy day.|听起来挺忙的。
[04:46.04]My daily routine is a bit different.|我的日常安排有点不一样。
[04:48.36]Every morning, I plan my lessons, then I teach students.|每天早上我备课，然后上课。
[04:54.54]After lunch, I teach more classes and sometimes have meetings with other teachers.|午饭后我继续上课，有时和其他老师开会。
[05:00.14]I usually finish my workday around 4 p.m.|我一般下午四点左右下班。
[05:04.04]That sounds like a fulfilling day, Paul.|听起来很充实，Paul。
[05:07.36]So remember, when you talk about your routine, think about when you start and finish,|记住，聊日常时要想：几点上班下班、
[05:13.56]what tasks you do, and if you have breaks or talk to colleagues.|做什么任务，以及有没有休息、和同事聊天。
[05:19.42]Yes, it makes your description complete.|对，这样描述才完整。
[05:23.16]Next, let's talk about your work environment.|接下来聊你的工作环境。
[05:27.12]This is where you work.|也就是你在哪儿工作。
[05:28.78]Is it an office, remote, hybrid, or outdoors?|是办公室、远程、混合办公，还是户外？
[05:33.82]Ah, yes.|啊对。
[05:34.76]This is very common now.|现在这很常见。
[05:37.20]Many people work remotely from home, like us sometimes.|很多人远程在家工作，我们有时也是。
[05:41.02]That's right.|没错。
[05:41.76]Or you can say, I work in an office downtown.|或者你可以说「I work in an office downtown.」
[05:46.06]Or I have a hybrid job.|或者「I have a hybrid job.」
[05:48.54]So I work some days at home and some days at the office.|也就是几天在家、几天在公司。
[05:53.08]And some people work outdoors, like a construction worker or a park ranger.|也有人做户外工作，比如建筑工人或公园管理员。
[05:59.08]I work outdoors. It's very nice.|我就在户外工作，挺不错的。
[06:02.46]That's true. And what about the atmosphere?|是这样。那氛围呢？
[06:06.08]Is it a formal or informal workplace?|是正式的还是非正式的工作环境？
[06:09.22]Good question.|好问题。
[06:10.46]A formal workplace usually means you wear a suit, and there are many rules.|正式的工作环境通常要穿西装，规矩也多。
[06:16.80]An informal workplace is more relaxed.|非正式的环境更放松，
[06:19.90]Maybe you can wear jeans.|也许可以穿牛仔裤。
[06:21.98]My workplace is usually informal.|我的工作环境一般比较随意，
[06:24.80]We can wear comfortable clothes.|可以穿舒服的衣服。
[06:27.18]Mine too. I love that.|我也是，我很喜欢。
[06:29.26]And how are your relationships with co-workers?|你和同事的关系怎么样？
[06:32.70]Are they friendly? Do you work closely together?|他们友好吗？你们配合紧密吗？
[06:36.28]Very important.|非常重要。
[06:37.44]I can say my co-workers are very friendly and we often help each other.|我可以说「My co-workers are very friendly and we often help each other.」
[06:43.70]Or I work in a small team and we are like a family.|或者「I work in a small team and we are like a family.」
[06:48.50]That's so nice to hear.|听着真好。
[06:50.04]And we have some useful vocabulary for this section, like open space.|这一部分还有些实用词汇，比如「open space」。
[06:55.84]That's a big office room with many desks, no separate rooms.|指有很多工位、没有隔间的大办公区。
[07:00.60]Yes, many companies have open spaces now.|对，现在很多公司都是开放式办公。
[07:04.00]Another word is deadline.|另一个词是「deadline」，
[07:05.72]This means you need to finish something by a specific time.|意思是必须在某个时间点前完成某件事。
[07:10.70]I have a deadline next week.|「I have a deadline next week.」
[07:13.84]Yes, deadlines can be stressful sometimes.|对，截止日期有时会让人有压力。
[07:17.50]And we have boss.|还有「boss」，
[07:19.90]That's the person who manages you.|就是管你的人。
[07:22.50]Coworker.|「Coworker」，
[07:23.44]That's your colleague, the person you work with.|就是同事，和你一起工作的人。
[07:26.36]And client.|还有「client」，
[07:27.54]That's a customer or a company you work for.|指客户，或者你服务的公司。
[07:30.74]Then there's team, a group of people working together.|还有「team」，一起工作的一群人。
[07:35.10]Yes, like we are working on a new project.|对，比如「我们在做一个新项目」。
[07:38.52]And finally, flexible hours.|最后是「flexible hours」，
[07:41.28]This means you can choose when you start and finish your workday within some limits.|指在一定范围内，你可以自己选择上班和下班时间。
[07:47.16]That's a great perk.|这是个很好的福利。
[07:48.94]So remember, you can talk about where you work, the atmosphere, and your co-workers.|记住，你可以聊工作地点、氛围和同事。
[07:54.52]Now, let's talk about something very personal.|现在聊点很个人的东西：
[07:58.48]Job satisfaction.|工作满意度。
[08:00.66]Do you like your job, Emily?|你喜欢你的工作吗，Emily？
[08:02.34]Oh, I love my job, Paul. It's so much fun to talk to our listeners and share English with them.|哦，我很爱我的工作，Paul。和听众聊天、分享英语特别有意思。
[08:10.65]So for me, I can say, I love my job because it's creative and I meet many interesting people.|所以我可以这样说：「I love my job because it's creative and I meet many interesting people.」
[08:18.78]That's wonderful, Emily. And that's exactly how you can express if you like your job.|太棒了，Emily。喜欢工作就可以这样表达。
[08:25.70]You can also say, I like my job because it's challenging.|也可以说「I like my job because it's challenging.」
[08:30.34]Or I like my job because the people are nice.|或者「I like my job because the people are nice.」
[08:34.64]What about the things you enjoy most or least? Sometimes there are parts of the job we don't like so much.|那最喜欢和最不喜欢的部分呢？工作里总有些不太喜欢的环节。
[08:43.36]That's true. For me, I enjoy teaching the most.|确实。对我来说，我最喜欢上课。
[08:47.61]It's so rewarding to see students learn. What I enjoy least sometimes is grading papers.|看到学生学会东西特别有成就感。我最不喜欢的是改作业，
[08:55.57]It can take a long time.|有时候很花时间。
[08:57.74]I understand. For me, I love interacting with our audience the most.|我理解。我最喜欢和观众互动，
[09:03.90]What I enjoy least is sometimes the technical side of things, like editing videos.|最不喜欢的是技术部分，比如剪视频，
[09:11.32]It's not my favorite.|那不是我的强项。
[09:14.04]We all have those parts, right? And sometimes people don't like their job, and they would like to change jobs.|每个人都有这样的部分，对吧？有时人们不喜欢现在的工作，想换工作。
[09:21.94]Yes, that's a very common feeling. You can say, I'm looking for a new opportunity.|对，这种感受很常见。你可以说「I'm looking for a new opportunity.」
[09:28.41]This means you want a new job.|意思是你想找一份新工作。
[09:31.24]Or, I want to find a job with better pay. Or, I want a job that is closer to my home.|或者「I want to find a job with better pay.」，再或者「I want a job that is closer to my home.」
[09:39.32]We have some more useful expressions here. It can be stressful sometimes, but this is a good way to talk about the difficulties, but also the positive things.|这里还有更多实用表达。聊工作有时会有压力，但这是谈论困难、同时也谈优点的好方式。
[09:49.62]For example, my job can be stressful sometimes, but I love the team I work with.|比如「My job can be stressful sometimes, but I love the team I work with.」
[09:56.70]Perfect. So when you talk about job satisfaction, think about if you like your job, what you enjoy, and if you want to change jobs.|很好。聊工作满意度时，想想：你喜欢这份工作吗、你喜欢什么、你想换工作吗。
[10:07.22]Okay, Paul, let's go back in time a little. Let's talk about past jobs and experience.|好，Paul，我们往回看一点，聊聊过去的工作和经历。
[10:13.70]Where did you work before?|你以前在哪儿工作？
[10:16.38]Ah, my previous jobs.|啊，我以前的工作。
[10:19.34]I can say, I used to work in a small company, but now I'm in a large international team.|我可以说「I used to work in a small company, but now I'm in a large international team.」
[10:27.36]This shows your career path.|这能体现你的职业轨迹。
[10:29.82]That's a great way to put it.|这个说法很好。
[10:32.32]Or, before this, I was a student and I worked part-time at a coffee shop.|或者「Before this, I was a student and I worked part-time at a coffee shop.」
[10:38.00]And what about what you learned in previous positions?|那你在之前的岗位上学到了什么？
[10:42.46]This is important for new jobs.|这对找新工作很重要。
[10:44.18]Yes, it show your skills. I can say, in my last job, I learned a lot about customer service.|对，这能体现你的能力。我可以说「In my last job, I learned a lot about customer service.」
[10:53.68]Or, I learned how to manage a team.|或者「I learned how to manage a team.」
[10:57.80]Very good. And this helps describe your career path so far. It's like a story of your jobs.|很好。这能描述你到目前为止的职业轨迹，就像一部工作故事。
[11:04.18]Exactly. So, if someone asks about your experience, you can tell them about your old jobs and what you learned.|正是。所以有人问你的经历时，可以讲讲以前的工作和收获。
[11:12.46]Like, I used to be a salesperson, and I learned how to talk to many different people.|比如「I used to be a salesperson, and I learned how to talk to many different people.」
[11:18.38]That's a valuable skill.|这是很值钱的能力。
[11:20.46]So remember, you can talk about where you worked before, what you learned, and your career path.|记住，你可以聊以前在哪儿工作、学到了什么，以及你的职业轨迹。
[11:27.16]Now, let's look to the future.|现在，我们看向未来。
[11:29.72]This is exciting.|这让人兴奋。
[11:31.20]Let's talk about future career goals.|聊聊未来的职业目标。
[11:34.42]Where do you see yourself in the future, Emily?|你觉得自己未来会在哪里，Emily？
[11:37.68]Hmm, good question, Paul.|嗯，好问题，Paul。
[11:39.48]I can say in the future I'd like to manage my own YouTube channel full-time.|我可以说「In the future I'd like to manage my own YouTube channel full-time.」
[11:45.44]That's a dream.|这是个梦想。
[11:46.92]Wow, that's a fantastic goal, Emily.|哇，太棒的目标了，Emily。
[11:49.06]And that's a perfect way to express it.|这是表达它的完美方式。
[11:51.88]Or you can say I want to become an expert in my field.|或者可以说「I want to become an expert in my field.」
[11:56.42]And what about skills you want to learn?|那你想学的技能呢？
[11:58.96]This shows you want to grow.|这能体现你想成长。
[12:00.58]Yes, I can say I want to improve my communication skills.|对，我可以说「I want to improve my communication skills.」
[12:05.68]Or I want to learn more about digital marketing.|或者「I want to learn more about digital marketing.」
[12:09.48]It shows you are always learning.|这说明你一直在学习。
[12:11.80]That's a great mindset.|这是很好的心态。
[12:13.42]And finally, your dream job.|最后，你的理想工作。
[12:15.74]What is your ultimate dream job, Paul?|你最终的理想工作是什么，Paul？
[12:18.22]Oh, my dream job is to travel the world and teach English in different countries.|哦，我的理想工作是环游世界，在不同国家教英语。
[12:24.74]That would be amazing.|那太棒了。
[12:26.44]That sounds like a wonderful adventure.|听起来是场美妙的冒险。
[12:28.64]My dream job is to create content that inspires millions of people.|我的理想工作是创作能激励数百万人的内容。
[12:33.98]That's lovely, Emily.|真好，Emily。
[12:35.52]So when you talk about your future goals, think about where you want to be, what skills you want to learn, and your dream job.|聊未来目标时，想想：你想去到哪里、想学什么技能，以及你的理想工作。
[12:44.52]Okay, Paul, we've talked a lot about our jobs.|好，Paul，我们聊了很多自己的工作。
[12:47.56]Now let's talk about how to ask someone else about their job.|现在聊聊怎么问别人的工作。
[12:51.54]This is super useful for real conversations.|这在真实对话里超级实用。
[12:54.42]Yes, very practical.|对，很实用。
[12:55.66]The most common question is, what do you do?|最常见的问题就是「What do you do?」
[12:59.04]Simple and direct.|简单直接。
[13:00.52]Exactly.|正是。
[13:01.36]And after they tell you their job, you can ask, do you like your job?|对方说完工作后，你可以问「Do you like your job?」
[13:06.20]This shows interest.|这表示你感兴趣。
[13:07.56]Yes, it's a nice follow-up question.|对，这是很好的追问。
[13:09.94]Another good one is, how long have you worked there?|另一个好问题是「How long have you worked there?」
[13:13.06]This tells you about their experience.|这能了解对方的资历。
[13:15.22]Like, oh, I've worked there for five years.|比如：「哦，我在那儿干了五年。」
[13:17.76]And then, to make the conversation more interesting, you can ask, what's the most interesting part of your job?|然后，想让对话更有意思，可以问「What's the most interesting part of your job?」
[13:24.76]That's a great question, Emily.|这问题很好，Emily。
[13:26.96]It opens up for a more detailed answer.|能引出更详细的回答。
[13:29.02]Or you can ask, what is a typical day like for you?|或者问「What is a typical day like for you?」
[13:33.02]Yes, or what do you do on a typical day?|对，或者「What do you do on a typical day?」
[13:36.52]These questions help you understand their work better and keep the conversation flowing.|这些问题能帮你更好地了解对方的工作，也让对话顺畅进行。
[13:40.74]So, if you meet someone new, remember these questions to start a friendly conversation about their job.|所以遇到新朋友时，记住这些问题，就能友好地聊起对方的工作。
[13:48.90]Wow, Paul. We covered so much today.|哇，Paul。今天我们讲了好多。
[13:52.12]From describing your job to talking about future goals and even asking others about their work.|从描述你的工作，到聊未来目标，甚至问别人的工作情况。
[13:58.26]I think our listeners have a lot of new words and phrases now.|我觉得听众们现在掌握了不少新词和短语。
[14:02.62]I agree, Emily.|我同意，Emily。
[14:03.72]This episode is packed with useful information for anyone wanting to talk about their job in English.|这一集塞满了实用内容，适合任何想用英语聊工作的人。
